# IYDT-GSRP acoustic analyses

These decks infer SUGAR log-yield and HOB from two acoustic response channels.
Application data and code are configured at the IYDT-GSRP level; no additional
phenomenology-prior link is used by the shipped acoustic decks.

## Analyses

| Directory | Type | Decks |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `I-SUGAR-hob-0` | two-stage rapid assessment | `runMPEM.r`, `runMPEM_0.r` |
| `I-SUGAR-hob` | complete joint assessment | `runMPEM.r` |

Run the rapid case from its directory:

```text
R CMD BATCH runMPEM.r runMPEM.out &
```

After the background calibration finishes successfully:

```text
cp .RData .RData-calibration
R CMD BATCH runMPEM_0.r runMPEM_0.out &
```

The calibration produces `opt.RData`, which is required under an exact renamed
path by the `2-Phen-sa` and `4-Phen` shipped decks. Retain
`.RData-calibration` as a pristine workspace for future event analyses; never
use an event-modified `.RData` as the saved calibration.

Run the complete case with only `runMPEM.r`. Docker names are
`IYDT-gsrp/Acoustic/I-SUGAR-hob-0` and
`IYDT-gsrp/Acoustic/I-SUGAR-hob`. Docker snapshots application code/data and
maintains a pristine rapid-calibration checkpoint automatically.

Review Bayesian, sampler, sample-count, worker-count, and seed settings before
production use. Confirm completion from the transcript and process status, not
merely from the presence of `.RData`.
